add(1,'b',3,3,'Explain','Explain why Date of birth has been separated into three fields.',ctx1,[4],'Avoid locale ambiguity;validateparts;source makes unsupported DATE performance/validation claims.','B',['A3.2.3'],'Retain date consistency reasoning while replacing form-specific separation with proper database datatype selection.','Explain why a database should store birth dates using a suitable date type and an unambiguous input convention,rather than arbitrary text such as03/04/2010.','Ambiguous text may mean3April or4March;consistent parsing into a date type gives the same intended date and allows meaningful date comparisons rather than text ordering.','Identifies day/month ambiguity.|Consistent input parsing/date representation prevents inconsistent interpretations.|Date-aware comparison/validation is preferable to arbitrary text operations.',issues=['SourceMS suggests DATE types inherently slower/harder to validate than split integers;not imported.'])
add(1,'c',4,6,'Explain','Explain two reasons why medical information should not be stored in the Person table.',ctx1,[5],'Separate repeated conditions for normalization and restrict sensitive data access.','B',['A3.2.5','A3.3.5'],'Keep normalization and view-based security,not unsupported general legal assertions.','A clinic stores Patient(PatientID,Name) and Condition(PatientID,ConditionCode,Notes). A patient may have many conditions. Explain why separate condition rows are preferable to Condition1,Condition2,… columns,and how a database view can limit what reception staff see.','Separate rows model an arbitrary number of conditions without repeating columns and avoid duplicated patient facts. A view can expose only ID/name while excluding medical notes,with permissions preventing direct access to underlying sensitive tables.','Recognizes repeated condition columns/repeating group.|Separate related rows support arbitrary condition count.|Avoids repeated patient details/update anomalies.|View exposes only permitted columns/records.|Medical notes excluded from reception view.|Underlying table access must also be restricted,so view is not bypassed.')
add(1,'d',4,4,'Outline','Outline two issues caused by storing redundant data.',ctx1,[5],'Update anomalies and storage waste/inconsistent copies.','A',['A3.2.5'],'Data duplication and dependency concerns explicit.','Outline two problems when a supplier address is copied into every product record.','A changed address may be updated in only some copies,creating inconsistent contacts;many repeated addresses consume extra storage and repeated update work.','Repeated update work or inconsistent copies.|Explains one supplier change leaves contradictory addresses.|Extra redundant storage.|Explains cost grows with number of products/copies.')
