add(2,'d',4,4,'Explain','Explain how the DBMS ensures a seat is not booked by two people simultaneously.',ctx2,[6],'Concurrency control/locking/transaction isolation prevents double booking.','A',['A3.3.6'],'Isolation and reliable transactions explicit.','Explain how transaction isolation can prevent two clients from both confirming the last available seat.','The availability check and reservation update form a transaction;conflicting transactions are serialized or blocked/aborted. The second must recheck after the first commits and cannot confirm an already-booked seat.','Availability check/update treated as transaction.|Conflicting access controlled by lock/serialization/equivalent.|First successful booking changes seat state before second confirmation.|Second transaction rechecks/fails rather than double books.')
